  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. We have to calculate the current. We know that, a potential barrier across silicon diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d21cdd39-d3fb-4891-82b1-43ecf2e12439-image.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 182px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>R</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><mn>200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0115</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>So, the current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p>",
